WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.960 --> 00:00:02.760
- We won't call it quits.

00:00:02.760 --> 00:00:04.085
We'll call it the start.

00:00:04.085 --> 00:00:06.690
(keys clacking)
(bright orchestral music)

00:00:06.690 --> 00:00:10.920
- Please, don't talk to me

00:00:10.920 --> 00:00:11.970
no more, Padraic.

00:00:11.970 --> 00:00:14.070
- So obviously, you know,
I'd wanted to get Colin

00:00:14.070 --> 00:00:16.770
and Brendan back together
since "In Bruges" days,

00:00:16.770 --> 00:00:19.920
and I was sort of in a breakup-y
kind of situation back then

00:00:19.920 --> 00:00:23.700
and just trying to explore
the sadness of that, you know,

00:00:23.700 --> 00:00:26.370
as deeply sad as those things can be.

00:00:26.370 --> 00:00:29.163
- You used to be nice, or
did you never used to be?

00:00:32.453 --> 00:00:33.600
- [Waymond] I'm another version of him

00:00:33.600 --> 00:00:35.850
from another life path, another universe.

00:00:35.850 --> 00:00:38.010
I'm here because we need your help.

00:00:38.010 --> 00:00:40.980
- Very busy today, no time to help you.

00:00:40.980 --> 00:00:44.310
- We were grappling with the
question of how do we exist

00:00:44.310 --> 00:00:46.590
in the chaos and the noise of modern life?

00:00:46.590 --> 00:00:49.200
You know, like, how do you
make sense of any of it?

00:00:49.200 --> 00:00:51.690
- We live in a world where
we're constantly distracted

00:00:51.690 --> 00:00:53.790
by so many things, and one
of the only things we have

00:00:53.790 --> 00:00:55.923
to give each other is our attention.

00:00:59.640 --> 00:01:02.580
- You'll make your movies
and you will do your art

00:01:02.580 --> 00:01:04.590
and you'll remember how it hurt.

00:01:04.590 --> 00:01:06.120
So you know what I'm saying?

00:01:06.120 --> 00:01:08.490
- All of my films I consider
to be personal films,

00:01:08.490 --> 00:01:10.320
but I've never really made a movie

00:01:10.320 --> 00:01:12.900
that is about a lived
experience as opposed

00:01:12.900 --> 00:01:15.330
to just a metaphor to something else.

00:01:15.330 --> 00:01:17.100
- I had never written
anything with anybody

00:01:17.100 --> 00:01:20.340
and I didn't know how,
whether it would work.

00:01:20.340 --> 00:01:21.690
I mean, it just sort of flowed out.

00:01:21.690 --> 00:01:23.640
It was really, it was a fascinating thing,

00:01:23.640 --> 00:01:25.023
and we had a blast.

00:01:27.692 --> 00:01:29.460
- You wanna dance the mask,

00:01:29.460 --> 00:01:31.530
you must service the composer.

00:01:31.530 --> 00:01:33.270
You gotta sublimate yourself, your ego,

00:01:33.270 --> 00:01:35.040
and yes, your identity.

00:01:35.040 --> 00:01:38.190
- The old saying inspiration
is, you know, 90% sweat.

00:01:38.190 --> 00:01:40.800
Incredible thing's gonna happen
when people come together

00:01:40.800 --> 00:01:42.780
and they're all aligned for the same aim.

00:01:42.780 --> 00:01:44.100
You have a chance then.

00:01:44.100 --> 00:01:46.440
There's a lot of people
that work very, very hard.

00:01:46.440 --> 00:01:48.840
You know, inspiration
is important, obviously,

00:01:48.840 --> 00:01:50.430
but there's a certain
point where you just have

00:01:50.430 --> 00:01:51.363
to be very lucky.

00:01:56.183 --> 00:01:59.430
- If today was your last day alive,

00:01:59.430 --> 00:02:02.280
what would you wish for?
- I have no idea.

00:02:02.280 --> 00:02:05.550
- I almost look at filmmaking as like,

00:02:05.550 --> 00:02:07.740
putting up sociological experiments

00:02:07.740 --> 00:02:11.460
and trying to make an
interesting example when we fail,

00:02:11.460 --> 00:02:12.690
why do we fail?

00:02:12.690 --> 00:02:14.490
- Never argue with an idiot.

00:02:14.490 --> 00:02:16.800
that'll only bring you down to their level

00:02:16.800 --> 00:02:19.353
and beat you with experience.

00:02:19.353 --> 00:02:22.853
(bright orchestral music)

